  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "narration_text": "Hi, my name is Ushasvi Rachel, and this video is about why machine-learning datasets are split into training, validation, and test sets.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "drawon",
        "visual_intent": "Presenter introduction and three-way split.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "intro"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "narration_text": "Start with a simple question. If a model performs well on the data it learned from, does that mean it will perform well on new data? Not necessarily. Training performance alone cannot tell us how well the model generalizes.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "divergence",
        "visual_intent": "Training success versus unseen-data question.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "question"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.12,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "narration_text": "That is why machine-learning data is usually separated into subsets with different jobs. The training set supports learning. Validation supports model choices. The test set provides a final independent check of the selected workflow.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Large dataset grid dividing into three functional groups.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "why"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:54:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.87,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "narration_text": "The training set is the data used to fit the model. From these examples, the model learns parameters, patterns, or decision boundaries. In short: training data goes in, and the model learns.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "flow",
        "visual_intent": "Training data flows into learned model.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "training"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.25,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "narration_text": "The validation set helps compare modeling choices without using the final test set. It may guide hyperparameters, candidate models, thresholds, early stopping, or configurations. Some workflows use cross-validation instead of one fixed validation split.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Validation choices and cross-validation caveat.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "validation"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.24,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "narration_text": "The test set is used for a final evaluation on data that did not fit the model or repeatedly guide model selection. Train means learn. Validate means choose or tune. Test means final check.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "flow",
        "visual_intent": "Train learn, validate choose, test final-check map.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "test"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.31,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "narration_text": "During development, teams may cycle between training and validation while improving the workflow. The test set should sit outside that loop. If test results repeatedly drive changes, the team can gradually adapt the system to that particular test set.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 18,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "branch",
        "visual_intent": "Train-validation loop beside protected test set.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "loop"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "narration_text": "Training performance describes behavior on data the model learned from. Generalization performance asks how it behaves on new observations from the target environment. These are different questions, and a large gap between them is a warning.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "divergence",
        "visual_intent": "Training and generalization performance comparison.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "performance"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.3,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "narration_text": "Overfitting is one reason this gap appears. A model can fit the training set extremely well while learning details that do not transfer to new data. Independent evaluation helps reveal that problem.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "curve",
        "visual_intent": "Simple overfitting curve and unseen-performance decline.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "overfit"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.89,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "narration_text": "Imagine a dataset with one thousand examples. A project might divide them into training, validation, and test groups. That is only an illustration. No percentage split is universally correct.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "isotype",
        "visual_intent": "Illustrative 1,000-example split without fixed percentages.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "example"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.93,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "narration_text": "The right strategy depends on dataset size, the task, temporal structure, class imbalance, how the data was collected, and the evaluation design. A split that works in one project may be misleading in another.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Six factors affecting split design.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "depends"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.87,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "narration_text": "Time-series data needs special care. Randomly mixing future and past observations can create an unrealistic evaluation. For forecasting or other temporal tasks, training should generally respect time order, with later observations used for evaluation.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "timeline",
        "visual_intent": "Past-to-future time-respecting split.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "time"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "narration_text": "Grouped or repeated observations also matter. Records from the same person, patient, customer, device, or SKU may need to stay together, depending on the task. Otherwise, information about one underlying entity can appear in both training and evaluation. Poor splitting can create leakage when information unavailable in real deployment influences the process.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "groups",
        "visual_intent": "Entity records kept together and leakage warning.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "groups"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B12.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 24.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "narration_text": "Cross-validation rotates which observations play the training and validation roles across multiple folds. This can make model selection more stable, especially with limited data. But cross-validation does not automatically solve time order, grouping, leakage, or final test evaluation.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 18,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "rotate",
        "visual_intent": "Four rotating cross-validation folds.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "cv"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B13.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 18.67,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B13.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B14",
      "narration_text": "The final test set should remain relatively untouched until major modeling decisions are complete. Validation helps make those decisions; testing evaluates the selected workflow. Reusing the test set weakens that final check. And even a protected test score cannot guarantee future production performance, because deployment data may differ.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "threshold",
        "visual_intent": "Protected test set, reuse warning, and deployment caveat.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "protected"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B14.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B14.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 21.61,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B14.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsExplainer",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:00:08"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B15",
      "narration_text": "Training data teaches the model, validation data helps us make modeling choices, and test data helps us evaluate whether those choices generalize to unseen examples.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Final three-card role summary and exact takeaway.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsExplainer",
          "props": {
            "kind": "takeaway"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B15.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T13:43:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B15.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.16,
      "build": {
